00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.440
- [Instructor] If the angles
A, B and C of a triangle

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.068
are in an arithmetic progression,

00:00:05.068 --> 00:00:08.500
and if a, b and c, lowercase, a, b and c,

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.380
denote the lengths of the
sides opposite to the capital,

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:14.960
the angles A, capital A, capital B

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:16.460
and capital C respectively,

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:20.030
then what is the value of this
expression right over here?

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:22.890
So let's see if we can
work our way through this.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.390
So let's just draw the triangle

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:25.760
just so we have a visualization

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.283
of what all of the letters represent.

00:00:27.283 --> 00:00:29.980
So we have the angles A, B, and C,

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.490
so let me just draw them like this.

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:37.070
So we have the angles A, B, and C.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.940
And then the sides opposite
them are the lowercase version.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:43.039
So the side opposite to
capital A is lowercase a,

00:00:43.039 --> 00:00:46.760
the side opposite to
capital B is lowercase b,

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:51.760
and the side opposite to the
angle capital C is lowercase c.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:53.754
Now the first piece of
information they tell us

00:00:53.754 --> 00:00:57.840
is that the angles capital
A, capital B, and capital C

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:01.007
of the triangle are in
arithmetic progression.

00:01:01.007 --> 00:01:06.007
Arithmetic progression, very fancy word,

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.150
but on arithmetic progression is,

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:09.963
is a series of numbers that are separated

00:01:09.963 --> 00:01:11.570
by the same amount.

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:13.391
So let me give you some examples.

00:01:13.391 --> 00:01:16.540
So one, two, three, that's
an arithmetic progression.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:20.100
Two, four, six arithmetic progression.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.150
Were separated by two every time.

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:26.830
I could do 10, 20, 30, also
an arithmetic progression.

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:28.380
These are all arithmetic progression.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:31.850
So all they're saying is, is
to go from angle A to angle B,

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:34.220
however much that is it's
the same amount to go

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:36.330
from angle B to angle C.

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:39.090
So let's see what that tells us,

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:40.500
what that tells us about,

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.160
or maybe tells us maybe it doesn't tell us

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:43.980
anything about those angles.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:48.290
So if we could say we have angle A

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:51.350
and then we have the notion angle B.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:56.064
So we could say that B is
equal to A plus some constant.

00:01:56.064 --> 00:01:57.190
We don't know what that is.

00:01:57.190 --> 00:01:58.870
It could go up by one, it could go by two,

00:01:58.870 --> 00:01:59.703
it could go by 10.

00:01:59.703 --> 00:02:00.990
We don't know what it is.

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:03.150
So A plus N.

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:07.188
