00:12:37.478 --> 00:12:40.220
as just turning this into b squared.

00:12:40.220 --> 00:12:42.750
Now, what does this give us?

00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:45.800
Well, we have this term right over here.

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:48.900
This term right over here is
now the exact same thing as

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:50.060
that over there.

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:55.060
So it is now a squared plus
b squared minus c squared.

00:12:55.190 --> 00:12:59.560
And then this term right over
here is now the exact same

00:12:59.560 --> 00:13:00.940
thing as this thing over here,

00:13:00.940 --> 00:13:03.024
which is the same thing as
that we're using the law of

00:13:03.024 --> 00:13:08.024
cosines. So this is plus
c squared plus b squared,

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:11.170
minus a squared.

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:12.470
And then all of that times,

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:17.059
this sine of B sine of
capital B over b squared.

00:13:17.059 --> 00:13:19.150
Now, what does this
give us the, we have an,

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:20.810
a squared and a negative a squared

00:13:20.810 --> 00:13:22.770
things are starting to simplify,

00:13:22.770 --> 00:13:25.380
a squared negative a squared.

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:29.400
We have a negative c squared
and a positive c squared.

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:30.380
So what are we left with?

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:32.640
We're just left with two b squared.

00:13:32.640 --> 00:13:37.210
So our whole expression has
simplified to two b squared sine

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:42.210
of B sine of capital B
over lowercase b squared.

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:46.720
These cancel out. So our whole
expression simplifies to,

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:49.830
two sine of B.

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:52.540
And from, from the get
go, we knew what B was.

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:53.870
We know it's 60 degrees.

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:58.870
So this is equal to two
times the sine of 60 degrees.

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:01.990
And if you don't have the
sine of 60 degrees memorize,

00:14:01.990 --> 00:14:05.390
you can always just break
out a 30, 60, 90 triangle.

00:14:05.390 --> 00:14:06.940
So let me draw.

00:14:06.940 --> 00:14:09.010
This is a right triangle, right over here.

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:12.150
This is 60 degrees
hypotenuse has length one.

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:14.160
We're dealing with the unit circle.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:16.090
The, the side is 30 degrees.

00:14:16.090 --> 00:14:16.923
The side opposite.

00:14:16.923 --> 00:14:19.760
The 30 degrees is one
half the side opposite.

00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:21.703
The 60 degrees is squared
of three times that so it's

00:14:21.703 --> 00:14:23.110
squared three over two.

00:14:23.110 --> 00:14:25.560
You can even use the Pythagorean
theorem to figure out

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:26.470
once you know one of them,

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:27.860
you could figure out the other one.

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:31.560
So it's the sine of sine is
opposite over hypotenuse.

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:33.186
So square to three over two over one,

00:14:33.186 --> 00:14:34.483
or it's just square to three over two.

00:14:34.483 --> 00:14:38.290
So this is equal to two, two times.

00:14:38.290 --> 00:14:39.260
There's a home stretch.

00:14:39.260 --> 00:14:43.690
It's very exciting square
root of three over two,

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:44.720
these cancel out.

00:14:44.720 --> 00:14:49.720
So we are left with the
square root root of three.

00:14:49.840 --> 00:14:51.870
That's a, that's a pretty neat problem.

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:52.880
And just in case, you're curious,

